Licenses for consumption on-premises shall only be issued to persons who manage and operate a: (i) restaurant; or (ii) nonprofit club.
(1) Restaurant. A restaurant means an established place of business actively in operation within Oglethorpe County where meals with substantial entrees selected by the customer from a full menu are served during all hours of operation with:
a. A full-service kitchen;
b. The serving of such meals being the principal business conducted, with the serving of alcoholic beverages to be consumed on the premises as only incidental thereto; and
c. A minimum serving schedule of at least two meals a day for at least five days a week, with the exception of recognized holidays, reasonable vacation time, and periods of actual redecoration.
(2) Nonprofit club. A nonprofit club means any nonprofit association organized under the laws of this state which:
a. Has been in existence and actively in operation within Oglethorpe County, Georgia, for at least one year immediately prior to the application for a license under this subdivision;
b. Is organized and exists primarily for civic, social, or charitable purposes;
c. Has members that participate and further the organization's purposes;
d. Owns or leases a building or space within a building for the reasonable use of its members; and
e. Has no member, officer, agent, or employee directly or indirectly receiving in the form of salary or other compensation, any profits from the sale of alcoholic beverages beyond a fixed salary.
(Ord. of 2-4-2019)

